+// sandboxGateObserver is a TEST SEAM (hk-dqo9u), the direct analog of
+// substrateRunnerObserver and for the same reason: the value we need to assert on
+// is unobservable in the DOT/review-loop test fixtures. Those fixtures use a
+// non-tmux substrate, so newPerRunSubstrate returns nil and the
+// perRunSubstrate.sandboxSpawn field the fix assigns can never be read back.
+// Observing the DECISION as it is made is observable regardless of substrate type.
+//
+// Invoked at the DOT agentic launch site with the gate's verdict and the resolved
+// harness identity. hk-dqo9u was exactly a "the call is in the wrong lexical
+// place" defect — sandboxSpawnForRun sat inside the SessionIDCaptured branch, so
+// for claude (SessionIDMinted) it was never called at all and the sandbox failed
+// silently open. No unit test of the gate helper could catch that, because the
+// helper was correct; only its placement was wrong. This seam makes the call
+// site itself assertable. nil in production (zero overhead).
+var sandboxGateObserver func(agentType core.AgentType, spawn *SrtSpawnConfig)
+
+// notifySandboxGate invokes sandboxGateObserver if set. No-op in prod.
+func notifySandboxGate(agentType core.AgentType, spawn *SrtSpawnConfig) {
+	if sandboxGateObserver != nil {
+		sandboxGateObserver(agentType, spawn)
+	}
+}
